{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518101-new-umbral-realm-humanhome","id":1518101,"title":"New umbral realm: Humanhome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T16:32:03-07:00","id":1518101,"title":"New umbral realm: Humanhome","content":"This idea came from my own reading of Wolfhome, and the thought of how the lessons learned there are only one half of the Werewolf experience. So I thought, what if there was an umbral realm meant to help teach Werewolves to embrace there human half?<br /> <br /> This realm is called Humanhome, and in it the Garou or Fera becomes locked in hominid form and thinks they are nothing but a normal human. They blend into society effortlessly and work as if nothing was wrong.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is quickly shattered as some form of supernatural thing intrudes upon the mundane life. What exactly it is varies, but they are always in truth an Emenation of the realm. The Garou must fight against this threat with only the tools a normal human has. If they learn how to embrace there human side, they will triumph and leave the realm. If not, they will perish, or worse.<br /> <br /> The sort of stories run in this realm are like the Supernatural episode It\u2019s a Terrible life, or the first and fourth matrix movies.<br /> <br /> So thoughts and opinions on this idea people?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:46:26-07:00","id":1518104,"title":"","content":"While such a realm surely exists, I do feel that one of the biggest problems the Fera have is not the lack of a human perspective but an excess of human attitudes towards problems and problem solving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T16:56:12-07:00","id":1518105,"title":"","content":"The reason why there isn't &quot;another side&quot; that perfectly complements Wolfhome is very similar to why there's not a male-only tribe that's the opposite of the Black Furies, and why Kami notably don't have a struggle for Autonomy, unlike other Possessed. The writing is trying to say something about a non-equivalent difference in experiences, which in the case of Wolfhome is not necessarily very clear but mostly involves being made to rely on only what beasts can rely on in the face of humans having taken away their territory, killed off all their prey or carefully corralled them, and generally made the world into a sterile, controlled place with no room for anything but humans and what humans want.<br /> <br /> So what does this locale offer that isn't already in, say, the Atrocity Realm, CyberRealm, or Scar? All of these involve largely human experiences with being helpless in the realm of technological progression and industry, in the case of the latter two, or monster attacks, in the case of a given portion of Atrocity. There's no need to lock anyone in Homid or make them forget that they're shapeshifters because the character of those realms already involves a very different approach required to deal with its problems, rather than simply powering through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T20:24:54-07:00","id":1518124,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> hmm, I guess you are right. Honestly I was thinking that the red talons would be sent to this realm and really hate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T22:44:59-07:00","id":1518127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518101-new-umbral-realm-humanhome?p=1518124#post1518124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> hmm, I guess you are right. Honestly I was thinking that the red talons would be sent to this realm and really hate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's every trip to the city for them, minus the amnesia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-16T03:03:32-07:00","id":1518136,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> your right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}